  "question": {
    "text": "The sum of the series\n$2 \\times 1 \\times{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_4-3 \\times 2 \\times{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_5+4 \\times 3 \\times{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_6-5 \\times 4$ $\\times { }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_7+\\ldots+18 \\times 17 \\times{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_{20}$, is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "34",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& (1-\\mathrm{x})^{20}={ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_0-{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_1 \\mathrm{x}+{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_2 \\mathrm{x}^2 \\ldots . .+{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_{20} \\mathrm{x}^{20} \\\\\n& \\frac{(1-\\mathrm{x})^{20}}{\\mathrm{x}^2}=\\frac{{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_0}{\\mathrm{x}^2}-\\frac{{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_1}{\\mathrm{x}}+{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_2-{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_3 \\mathrm{x}+{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_4 \\mathrm{x}^2 \\ldots\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nDiff twice and put $\\mathrm{x}=1$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =6-{ }^{20} \\mathrm{C}_1(2)+\\mathrm{A} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~A}=40-6=34\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
